course: dictionary
lesson: 4914
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word immediate can mean happening at once, nearest, or needing attention now. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it, just as you did in the last lesson. The clues in the sentence show which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «I move that the meeting adjourn, for the immediate adoption of more energetic remedies,» says the Dodo. Here immediate means happening at once. The Dodo wants the meeting to stop and try something livelier straight away. Ask yourself: is there a delay, or does something need doing now? If yes, immediate means at once.
explain: Immediate has another meaning in everyday life. Your immediate family is the people closest to you, such as your parents, brothers and sisters. Here immediate means nearest in relationship. To check your choice, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Immediate means happening at once, with no delay.
fact: The adverb form is immediately, as in "She answered immediately."
fact: Immediate can also mean nearest in place, time or relationship, as in "the immediate area" or "immediate family".
fact: In safety advice, «seek immediate help» means get help right away.
fact: Useful phrases: immediate effect, immediate action, immediate danger.
exercise: «Seek immediate help if you feel unwell.» What does immediate mean here? | Long-lasting | Very large | Nearest in the street | *Right away, with no delay
exercise: Maya says, «My immediate family is coming to the party.» Who is in her immediate family? | Her teacher and her classmates | *Her parents, brothers and sisters | Everyone in the whole town
exercise: In exam and formal language, immediate often means what? | *Straight away | Very tall | Rather quiet | Far away
test: «The Dodo wanted immediate action, not a long talk.» What does immediate action mean? | Action that never ends | *Action taken straight away | Action taken slowly, over many weeks | Action taken only by birds
test: The sign says «Immediate danger: keep out.» What does immediate danger mean? | A danger that is pretend | A danger far away in the future | A danger only for animals | *A danger that is happening now
exam: What does immediate mean in «The shop's immediate area is full of cafes»? | *Nearest in place | Very cheap | Needing attention now | Happening at once
